{"id": "en_story_gimli", "tag": "AVIATION", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#FF9F43", "lang": "en", "total": 68.99, "segments": [{"text": "On 23 July 1983, Air Canada Flight 143 flies from Montreal to Edmonton with extreme danger.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.7}, {"text": "Ground crews calculate the fuel in pounds instead of kilograms by a massive human error.", "start": 6.26, "end": 9.82}, {"text": "The Boeing 767 carries only about 10,100 kg instead of the 22,300 kg truly needed.", "start": 10.4, "end": 16.16}, {"text": "At about 41,000 feet in the freezing air, both heavy jet engines suddenly stop working.", "start": 16.88, "end": 21.08}, {"text": "Every glass cockpit screen goes completely dark while sheer panic rises in the cabin.", "start": 21.54, "end": 25.14}, {"text": "The emergency ram air turbine drops out to awkwardly power the essential flight hydraulics.", "start": 25.72, "end": 29.34}, {"text": "The city of Winnipeg is much too far away for the dying passenger airplane.", "start": 29.34, "end": 32.7}, {"text": "First officer Maurice Quintal desperately remembers the former military air force base located at Gimli.", "start": 33.16, "end": 37.54}, {"text": "They discover the target runway is currently being used for a local car race.", "start": 37.94, "end": 40.98}, {"text": "Numerous campers and families are parked dangerously close to the active landing strip asphalt.", "start": 41.56, "end": 45.08}, {"text": "Captain Bob Pearson uses his glider pilot experience to perform a risky forward slip.", "start": 45.82, "end": 49.56}, {"text": "He aggressively maneuvers the heavy aircraft to rapidly lose unwanted height above the crowd.", "start": 49.9, "end": 53.34}, {"text": "The nose gear completely collapses on impact, causing the metal jet to scrape violently.", "start": 53.88, "end": 57.62}, {"text": "All 69 people survive the terrifying ordeal with only about 10 minor injuries reported.", "start": 58.18, "end": 62.34}, {"text": "Would you have trusted a glider pilot to land this doomed passenger jet safely?", "start": 62.86, "end": 65.84}], "words": [["On", 0.0, 0.28], ["23", 0.28, 0.62], ["July", 0.62, 0.96], ["1983,", 0.96, 1.76], ["Air", 2.08, 2.18], ["Canada", 2.18, 2.44], ["Flight", 2.44, 2.68], ["143", 2.68, 3.34], ["flies", 3.34, 3.6], ["from", 3.6, 3.78], ["Montreal", 3.78, 3.98], ["to", 3.98, 4.3], ["Edmonton", 4.3, 4.66], ["with", 4.66, 4.88], ["extreme", 4.88, 5.38], ["danger.", 5.38, 5.7], ["Ground", 6.26, 6.5], ["crews", 6.5, 6.68], ["calculate", 6.68, 7.08], ["the", 7.08, 7.24], ["fuel", 7.24, 7.38], ["in", 7.38, 7.52], ["pounds", 7.52, 7.8], ["instead", 7.8, 8.24], ["of", 8.24, 8.4], ["kilograms", 8.4, 8.68], ["by", 8.68, 8.94], ["a", 8.94, 9.04], ["massive", 9.04, 9.38], ["human", 9.38, 9.66], ["error.", 9.66, 9.82], ["The", 10.4, 10.58], ["Boeing", 10.58, 10.74], ["767", 10.74, 11.34], ["carries", 11.34, 11.72], ["only", 11.72, 11.98], ["about", 11.98, 12.2], ["10,100", 11.99, 11.131], ["kg", 12.0, 11.281], ["instead", 13.4, 13.86], ["of", 13.86, 13.98], ["the", 13.98, 14.06], ["22,300", 13.99, 12.383], ["kg", 14.0, 12.534], ["truly", 15.42, 15.84], ["needed.", 15.84, 16.16], ["At", 16.88, 17.1], ["about", 17.1, 17.26], ["41,000", 17.110000000000003, 14.037], ["feet", 17.84, 18.02], ["in", 18.02, 18.12], ["the", 18.12, 18.22], ["freezing", 18.22, 18.56], ["air,", 18.56, 18.86], ["both", 19.24, 19.36], ["heavy", 19.36, 19.56], ["jet", 19.56, 19.76], ["engines", 19.76, 19.92], ["suddenly", 19.92, 20.32], ["stop", 20.32, 20.7], ["working.", 20.7, 21.08], ["Every", 21.54, 21.8], ["glass", 21.8, 22.0], ["cockpit", 22.0, 22.32], ["screen", 22.32, 22.6], ["goes", 22.6, 22.8], ["completely", 22.8, 23.18], ["dark", 23.18, 23.52], ["while", 23.52, 23.74], ["sheer", 23.74, 23.98], ["panic", 23.98, 24.26], ["rises", 24.26, 24.66], ["in", 24.66, 24.84], ["the", 24.84, 24.94], ["cabin.", 24.94, 25.14], ["The", 25.72, 25.9], ["emergency", 25